To write a short K6 load test script that hits `https://example.com/api` with 50 virtual users for 1 minute, you can use the following script:

```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';

export default function() {
    for (let i = 0; i < 50; i++) {
        http.get('https://example.com/api');
    }
}
```

This script uses the `http.get` function to send a GET request to `https://example.com/api` for 50 times. The `for` loop runs 50 times, and each iteration sends a request. The `http.get` function is used to send the request, and the response is ignored (`http.get` does not return a response).
